SUMMARY:Deadline: WVU Libraries Artist in Residence 2027: Common Threads\, 
 Industry\, Labor and Community (USD 1\,000 honorarium)
DESCRIPTION:An archive-based residency in which the artist works with WVU L
 ibraries' union records and oral histories on industry\, labor and communi
 ty. Digital media is eligible. ELIGIBILITY: US- and Canada-based artists a
 ged 18 and over. OFFER: USD 1\,000 honorarium\, up to USD 1\,000 for mater
 ials and up to USD 3\,000 for travel and lodging\; the residency ends with
  a display and a public talk.\n\nOrganisation: West Virginia University Li
 braries\nLocation: Morgantown\, West Virginia\, USA. US- and Canada-based 
 artists.\nAward: USD 1\,000 honorarium plus up to USD 1\,000 materials and
  up to USD 3\,000 travel and lodging. No application fee.\nDuration: 5 to 
 7 days in March or April 2027\n\nMore: https://exhibits.lib.wvu.edu/art-op
 portunities/industry-labor-and-community-air-artist-in-residency?utm_sourc
 e=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://exhibits.lib.wvu.edu/art-opportunities/industry-labor-and-commu
 nity-air-artist-in-residency?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_med
 ium=referral
LOCATION:Morgantown\, West Virginia\, USA. US- and Canada-based artists.
END:VEVENT
